<title>USA: G&amp;K backs FY97 EPS view $1.34 vs $1.11.</title>
<headline>G&amp;K backs FY97 EPS view $1.34 vs $1.11.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>G&amp;K Services Inc said it is comfortable with the First Call consensus of analysts' forecasts for fiscal 1997 earnings of $1.34 per share, compared to $1.11 per share in fiscal 1996 ended in June.</p>
<p>Speaking at the annual meeting of the uniform and textile supply company on Thursday, chief executive Richard Fink said, &quot;We expect a strong year. We're comfortable with those (First Call) projections, though none of them are easy to accomplish.&quot;</p>
<p>Shares were unchanged at 28-1/4.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
